+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional `dueDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) and a computed `overdue` flag, filterable via `GET /todos?overdue=true|false` and shown on the list page with a „nur überfällige“ toggle.
+
+**Architecture:** All domain logic (validation, overdue computation against an injectable UTC clock, filtering) lives in `src/store.mjs`; `src/app.mjs` only parses/validates the `overdue` query parameter; `public/index.html` renders what the API returns and refetches with `?overdue=true` when the toggle is on.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, builtins only (`node:http`, `node:test`), plain HTML + ES module script.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-14-due-date-design.md` (ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` → HTTP 400.
+- TDD: failing test in `test/` first.
+- `dueDate`: `null` or string matching `^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$` that is a real calendar date; error message exactly `dueDate must be a date in YYYY-MM-DD format or null`.
+- Overdue: `!done && dueDate !== null && dueDate < today`, today = `now().toISOString().slice(0, 10)` (UTC). Due today is not overdue.
+- Bad `overdue` query value → 400 with message exactly `overdue must be true or false`.
+- UI copy exactly: `nur überfällige`, ` · fällig: TT.MM.JJJJ`, ` · überfällig`. New test ids: `overdue-filter`, `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`. No styling, no sorting.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Empty string `dueDate: ""` → 400 (not treated as „no date“). Test in Task 1.
+- Leap days: `2028-02-29` valid, `2026-02-29` invalid. Test in Task 1.
+- Failed PATCH applies nothing: `PATCH {title:'Neu', dueDate:'kaputt'}` → 400 and title unchanged. Test in Task 1.
+- Marking an overdue todo done makes `overdue` false (and it leaves the `?overdue=true` list). Test in Task 2.
+- `?overdue=` (empty) and `?overdue=TRUE` → 400 (strict, case-sensitive). Test in Task 2.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: `dueDate` and `overdue` in the store
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: `createStore({ now = () => new Date() } = {})`; every todo returned by `list`/`get`/`add`/`update` is a fresh object `{ id, title, done, dueDate, overdue }`; `list({ overdue } = {})` (filter used in Task 2).
+- Produces (tests): `withServer(fn, store = createStore())` — change the helper to accept a store and pass it to `createApp(store)`; import `createStore` from `../src/store.mjs`. Fixed clock constant `const fixedNow = () => new Date('2026-10-14T12:00:00Z');`.
+
