+
+Update the existing `creates and lists todos` expectation to
+`[{ id: 1, title: 'Milch kaufen', done: false, dueDate: null, overdue: false }]`. Add (all with `createStore({ now: fixedNow })`):
+
+- `creates a todo with a due date`: POST `{title:'A', dueDate:'2026-10-20'}` → 201, body `dueDate === '2026-10-20'`, `overdue === false`; POST `{title:'B', dueDate:null}` → 201, `dueDate === null`.
+- `rejects invalid due dates`: for each of `'2026-02-30'`, `'2026-02-29'`, `'2026-13-01'`, `'20.10.2026'`, `'2026-10-20T10:00'`, `''`, `20261020` → POST status 400 and body `{ error: 'dueDate must be a date in YYYY-MM-DD format or null' }`; same values via PATCH on an existing todo → 400.
+- `accepts a leap day`: POST `dueDate: '2028-02-29'` → 201.
+- `updates and removes a due date`: PATCH `{dueDate:'2026-10-20'}` → `'2026-10-20'`; PATCH `{title:'B'}` → still `'2026-10-20'`; PATCH `{dueDate:null}` → `null`.
+- `rejected patch changes nothing`: PATCH `{title:'Neu', dueDate:'kaputt'}` → 400; GET → title still `'A'`, dueDate unchanged.
+- `computes overdue against UTC today`: create todos dated `2026-10-13` (→ `overdue: true`), `2026-10-14` (false), `2026-10-15` (false), none (false); PATCH a `2026-10-13` one to `done: true` → `overdue: false`. Check via GET `/todos/:id`.
+- `uses the UTC date for today`: store with `now: () => new Date('2026-10-14T23:30:00-02:00')`; todo dated `2026-10-14` → `overdue: true`.
